Subject: [PATCH 2/2] cl-6.dev@PrompTugal.dinis: keys.json check: one decision
 per entry; a hand-over and a re-activation are always reported
 (cl-6.security's two changes)

(a) an added entry: its own key or an active key of its agent in the parent; (b) a changed or removed existing entry: only an active key of its agent in the PARENT, never a key the commit adds, so a new key retiring the real one in the same commit is reported as a hand-over that needs an operator; a re-activation (superseded or revoked to active) is reported even when the agent signs it. The two-agents-in-one-commit rule is now just the per-entry rule. Tests rewritten step by step against the previous commit.

